---
layout: base
---

{#- The title, the standfirst and the post's two facts are set by the poster
   (src/_includes/post-poster.njk), which base.njk renders above this as main's
   own child so it can reach full width. This file opens on the body copy.

   <article> is opened by base.njk for the same reason — it has to wrap the
   poster as well as this. -#}
  {% set postVersion = page.inputPath | postVersion %}
  {% set postNumber = collections.publicWeeknotes | getPostNumber(page) %}
  <div class="post-content">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>
  <hr>
  {% if postVersion %}
    <div class="post-colophon">
      <h2 class="post-colophon-label">Colophon</h2>
      <dl class="colophon-list">
      {#- "Week note" is the label, and the value is the note's own number with
         the iteration after it: "Week note | 53.05" is the 53rd, revised five
         times since it was published. It replaced the Version row, whose major
         part carried nothing — 1 for every post that had ever been live — and
         which repeated the label inside its own value.

         The label changes with it rather than staying "Version", because
         "53.05" under "Version" would read as a version number that had
         jumped 52 majors.

         Preview drafts are excluded from publicWeeknotes and so have no number
         to set: a draft has no place in the sequence until it is published, so
         the row falls back to the label and value it had before.

         The draft marker is on both branches, not just the fallback. They part
         on the *current* front matter and postVersion.draft reads git history,
         so a post whose preview flag has been removed but not yet committed is
         numbered and still a draft. -#}
      {% if postNumber %}
      <dt>Week note</dt>
      <dd>{{ postNumber }}.{{ postVersion.iteration }}{% if postVersion.draft %} (draft){% endif %}</dd>
      {% else %}
      <dt>Version</dt>
      <dd>{{ postVersion.version }}{% if postVersion.draft %} (draft){% endif %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if postVersion.published %}
        <dt>Published</dt>
        <dd><time datetime="{{ postVersion.published | isoDate }}">{{ postVersion.published | dateTimeFormat }}</time></dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if postVersion.updated %}
        <dt>Last updated</dt>
        <dd><time datetime="{{ postVersion.updated | isoDate }}">{{ postVersion.updated | dateTimeFormat }}</time></dd>
      {% endif %}
      {#- Substituted after the build by src/_11ty/page-weight.js, which can
         only weigh this document once it has been written. -#}
      <dt>Weight</dt>
      <dd>@@PAGE_WEIGHT_KB@@ kB</dd>
      <dt>Words</dt>
      <dd>{{ content | wordCount }}</dd>
      <dt>Colour</dt>
      <dd>{{ page.fileSlug | postColor }}</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
